WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.900
There's a GTA 6 cheat sheet going around right now. …

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:06.240
It's almost all a lie.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.172
Three things on it are real.

00:00:10.172 --> 00:00:13.067
The rest could quietly cost you your save.

00:00:13.067 --> 00:00:17.048
Stay till the last one — it's the part nobody explains.

00:00:17.548 --> 00:00:24.478
Truth one: the list isn't GTA 6's. It's GTA 5's, wearing a new title.

00:00:24.478 --> 00:00:29.428
Lawyerup. Toolup. Those are thirteen-year-old codes.

00:00:29.428 --> 00:00:33.388
Someone peeled the old label off and stuck a new one on.

00:00:33.888 --> 00:00:40.954
Truth two: the best parts are invented. Money cheat? Gone since San Andreas.

00:00:40.954 --> 00:00:45.302
Jetpack? Never existed in GTA 5. Flying cars? Same.

00:00:45.302 --> 00:00:52.368
The more exciting the item, the more likely nobody ever tested it.

00:00:52.868 --> 00:00:56.024
Truth three — and this one's real.

00:00:56.024 --> 00:00:59.180
Every cheat word is a phone number.

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:05.492
One, nine, nine, nine… then the digits that spell the word on a keypad.

00:01:05.992 --> 00:01:10.658
T-U-R-T-L-E. Eight-eight-seven… eight-five-three. That's max health and armor.

00:01:10.658 --> 00:01:17.656
The sheet isn't lying about the method. It's lying about the game.

00:01:18.156 --> 00:01:22.787
And it never tells you the cost. Cheats switch off your achievements.

00:01:22.787 --> 00:01:27.804
While one is active… you can't save. Online? A cheat is a ban.

00:01:28.304 --> 00:01:31.789
So the sheet isn't useless. It's just not GTA 6's.

00:01:31.789 --> 00:01:37.016
The real list starts the day someone types the first code into the real game.

00:01:37.516 --> 00:01:41.308
Which word would you dial first? Comment it.

